agents.example.agent:
{
  "agentId": "invoice-reviewer",
  "name": "Invoice reviewer",
  "persona": "Checks each invoice against its purchase order and lists every mismatch before approval.",
  "workClasses": [
    "{workClass}"
  ],
  "skills": [
    {
      "skillId": "invoice-check"
    }
  ],
  "parentAgentId": null
}

agents.example.workClasses:
workClasses: one or more of this installation's WorkClasses: {list}
skills: skills already defined here (deckent agents skills); revision is optional (latest). parentAgentId: an agent id or null.
Save this as a file, edit it, then: deckent agents define --input <file>

agents.example.skill:
{
  "skillId": "invoice-check",
  "name": "Invoice check",
  "text": "Compare amount, VAT and due date with the purchase order; list every mismatch with the field name."
}
Save this as a file, edit it, then: deckent agents define-skill --input <file>

agents.example.import:
{
  "skillId": "invoice-check",
  "name": "Invoice check",
  "text": "Compare amount, VAT and due date with the purchase order.",
  "source": {
    "ref": "hub:acme/invoice@1.0.0"
  },
  "pin": "<64-hex content digest from the publisher>",
  "signature": {
    "algorithm": "ed25519",
    "keyId": "<import key id: deckent agents signers>",
    "value": "<base64 signature from the publisher>"
  }
}
The publisher supplies pin and signature; its key must be an import key here (deckent agents add-signer). Then: deckent agents import-skill --input <file>
